# Sidekiq Jobs Guidelines

### Sidekiq Job Rules

#### When to Check These Rules
- When creating new background jobs
- When modifying existing jobs
- When implementing job retries
- When handling job errors

#### Rules
- Use Sidekiq exclusively (never use ActiveJob)
- Location: app/sidekiq
- Follow Sidekiq best practices
- Implement proper error handling
- Use appropriate retry strategies
- Consider job idempotency
- Handle job timeouts
- Use proper job naming
- Consider job priority

#### Examples
✅ Correct:
```ruby
class ProcessUserJob
  include Sidekiq::Job
  
  sidekiq_options queue: :high, retry: 3
  
  def perform(user_id)
    user = User.find(user_id)
    # Process user
  rescue ActiveRecord::RecordNotFound => e
    Rails.logger.error("User not found: #{user_id}")
    raise e
  end
end
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Using ActiveJob
- Not handling errors
- No retry strategy
- Not considering idempotency
- Poor job naming
- No queue specification

#### Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Using ActiveJob instead of Sidekiq
- Not handling errors properly
- No retry strategy
- Not considering idempotency
- Poor job organization
- No proper logging

#### Validation Checklist
- [ ] Using Sidekiq (not ActiveJob)
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] Appropriate retry strategy
- [ ] Job is idempotent
- [ ] Proper job naming
- [ ] Queue specified
- [ ] Timeout handling
- [ ] Proper logging
